Backlog tail, Selected item/items:
All confirmed. Here's the plan:

```text
1. Add write/delete capability to the disk port layer
    [ ] 'content/backend/core/engine_deps/ports.py': Add two abstract methods to DiskPort
        - write_file(tokenized_path: str, content: str) -> None — raises: InvalidPathToken, FileAccessError
        - delete_file(tokenized_path: str) -> None — raises: InvalidPathToken, NoSuchFile, FileAccessError
    [ ] 'content/backend/adapters/disk_adapter.py': Implement the two methods in LinuxDiskAdapter
        - write_file: resolve via _resolve_tokenized_path, create parent dirs, write_text; wrap PermissionError/UnicodeDecodeError as FileAccessError
        - delete_file: resolve via _resolve_tokenized_path, if not exists or not a file raise NoSuchFile; unlink; optionally rmdir empty parent chain up to base dir

2. Add a result type for the apply operation
    [ ] 'content/backend/core/engine_deps/result.py': New dataclass
        - IngestApplyResult with fields: written list[str], deleted list[str], errors list[str]
        - extends Result (so it fits the existing Result hierarchy)

3. Add apply_file_changes to IngestionServiceImpl
    [ ] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py': New method on IngestionServiceImpl
        - signature: apply_file_changes(raw_text: str) -> IngestApplyResult
        - regex-parse ¤filepath="X"¤ blocks (same pattern as git-ops receive)
        - handle ¤deletelist¤ section (same pattern as git-ops receive)
        - strip leading/trailing ``` fence lines from each file's content (mirror _clean_content)
        - prefix relative paths with <PUD>/ for tokenized resolution
        - call self.files.write_file / self.files.delete_file for each
        - collect successes and failures, return IngestApplyResult
        - do NOT do any git operations

4. Add /api/ingest endpoint to the server
    [ ] 'content/backend/server.py': New POST route
        - _handle_ingest: read JSON body { "content": "..." }
        - call self.server.ingestion.apply_file_changes(content)
        - serialize IngestApplyResult to JSON, send 200
        - send 400 if body malformed, 500 if unexpected exception
        - add to do_POST routing (alongside GPU_BOX_PATHS check)

5. Frontend: Alt+Enter handler and API client method
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/api-client.js': Add ingestFileChanges(content) method
        - POST /api/ingest with JSON body
        - return parsed JSON response
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/clanker-app.js': Wire up Alt+Enter
        - add 'Alt+Enter' to #inputActions (and #messageActions if relevant)
        - handler: get selected message content (same source as #copySelected reads from)
        - call apiClient.ingestFileChanges(content)
        - on success: toast like "3 files written, 1 deleted"
        - on error: toast with error message
        - do NOT copy to clipboard (that's still Ctrl+Enter only)
```
